      {
        "index": 2,
        "text": "He cut up a kind of seashell with a sharpened knife, and hammered it into powder on a skateboard, and made at most one gram, which was enough to accelerate one’s pulse until he or she died. This kind of poison can date back to 10,000 BC when people rubbed it on spears to kill beasts. The professor mixed the poison with onion, watermelon and yogurt for his wife.",
        "zh": "他用磨尖的刀切碎了一种贝壳，在滑板上把它锤成粉末，制成的量至多一克，按故事的说法，这足以使人的脉搏加快，直至死亡。这种毒物的使用可追溯到公元前一万年，当时人们把它涂在长矛上杀死野兽。教授把毒物与洋葱混在一起，又加上西瓜和酸奶，给妻子吃。",
